  \[
  d_w(x_q,x_i)=w\,|x_q-x_i|.
  \]
  \begin{enumerate}
    \item Re‑evaluate the distances for \(x_q=7\) and identify the three nearest neighbours under the scaled metric.
    \item Compute the corresponding prediction \(\hat y_w(7)\) and compare it with the original \(\hat y(7)=12\).
    \item Explain why multiplying the distance by a positive constant does (or does not) change the neighbour set and the resulting prediction.
  \end{enumerate}

  \item \textbf{Bias–variance trade‑off for different \(k\).}\\
  Using the original data set, qualitatively describe the expected bias and variance of the $k$‑NN regressor for:
  \begin{enumerate}
    \item a small value of \(k\) (e.g., \(k=1\));
