  \end{enumerate}
  Relate your discussion to the notions of under‑fitting and over‑fitting.

  \item \textbf{Assumptions underlying simple averaging.}\\
  List the statistical assumptions that make the plain average of the neighbour targets an unbiased estimator of \(\mathbb{E}[Y\mid X=x_q]\).  For each assumption, discuss what could happen if it is violated in practice (e.g., heteroscedastic noise, dependence between observations).

  \item \textbf{Influence of an outlier.}\\
  Assume the fourth training point is corrupted to \((x_4,y_4)=(11,30)\).
